Today, I learnt about:
- arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /, //, %, **)
- print() -> Used to display output on the screen
- type() -> Helps to identify the data type of a value.
Different data types: int, float, complex, str, list, dict, tuple

print("Hello World!") # print hello world 

print(2 + 3) # addition(+) 
print(3 - 1) # subtraction(-) 
print(2 * 3) # multiplication(*)  
print(3 / 2) # division(/) 
print(3 ** 2) # exponential(**) 
print(3 % 2) # modulus(%) 
print(3 // 2) # Floor division operator(//)

print(type(10)) # Int 
print(type(3.14)) # Float 
print(type(1 + 3j)) # Complex 
print(type('Febia')) # String 
print(type([1, 2, 3])) # List 
print(type({'name': 'Febia'})) # Dictionary 
print(type((2.2, 1, 3, 5.1))) # Tuple
